@0    = ~Muppets!! Them bloody muppets are everywhere!! Every wheres I say, every where! ARGGHH!!~
@1    = ~Ye muppet are ye not? If ye are I'll bloody thrash ye!~
@2    = ~Everywhere I go muppets! But beware of the muppet master he will get ye he will. Everywhere I say everywhere!!~
@3    = ~Off with ye little one I am far better then the likes of ye... Ye is a muppet yes? ARGHHH! ~
@4    = ~Do not touch me, I am super important!~
@5    = ~Wanna swig? Burrp!! I am really the elven god Corellon but I decided to visit you little people in elven form. Ughhh where's me elven wine?~
@6    = ~What? You again? Can't ya see I am like totally blizt?~
@7    = ~Now in all seriousness young Bhaalspawn, we will watch your career with great interest.~
@8    = ~Vel'uss? Plynn dosst iblith akh lueth z'bin!~
@9    = ~I do not understand you. Do you speak common?~
@10   = ~Opps sorry to bother you.~
@11   = ~Sarn waela iblith! Lit waela lueth waela ragar brorna lueth wund nind, kyorlin elghinn. Very well then. What is it you want <PRO_RACE> hmmm?~
@12   = ~What are two drow doing on the surface? Isn't it dangerous to be seen in the open like this?~
@13   = ~I just wanted to see if you could speak the common tongue besides that foul drow tongue.~
@14   = ~I would hardly call surfacers a threat wael. Perhaps they fear us more, which is why we were left alone until you came here and rudely interrupted our dinner. And our business here is that, *our* business. Well let me lay down a hint just for you, plus I will try and make it simple for you to comprehend. We are here observing someone and events that are unfolding as we speak. I will say nothing more. *Maybe* we will meet again. Now to use a quote you surfacers enjoy saying "Make like a bee and buzz off"!~
@15   = ~Ah yes, quite the response I would expect from surface trash. I would like to see you try and speak drow, but that matters not now. I will enjoy draining than consuming your blood! Lets dance shall we?~
@16   = ~By the Mistress of the Dead go away!~
@17   = ~Sorry about that.~
@18   = ~Die you drow bitch!~
@19   = ~May The Goddess of Death consume your soul!~
@20   = ~Greetings good, <SIRMAAM>. You have the appearance of an adventurer and I was wondering if you could help me out.~
@21   = ~We might be able to help you, what is the problem?~
@22   = ~Sorry, we do not have the time.~
@23   = ~Well it would seem I lost a valuable bust of the goddess of Mystra. I am so lost without her, she is my precious. Can you help me out in trying to find it?~
@24   = ~Sure we can. Do you have any details on how it disappeared?~
@25   = ~Well thanks anyway, return if you change your mind.~
@26   = ~I was traveling in the Temple District last night when suddenly out of no where, these thugs jumped me and knocked me out. Later I awoke with a nasty bump on my head and my bust missing. I will pay handsomely for its return if you find it.~
@27   = ~We'll start from there and return if we find out anything new.~
@28   = ~I see you have returned. Did you find my bust?~
@29   = ~No we did not. We'll continue searching now.~
@30   = ~Please find it and return when you have it.~
@31   = ~You return and have my bust of Mystra! I am most grateful for this. I shall give you 2000 gold for its safe return.~
@32   = ~Glad to see you again good <SIRMAAM>. I thank you once again in recovering my bust of Mystra for me.~
@33   = ~I used to be like, a world renown bard. Yep...everyone knew me across the globe. You like, want an autograph or something? Please?~
@34   = ~You ever get this like, sudden intense craving for something? I've gotta have like, something sweet. Maybe a banana?~
@35   = ~The current dialogue state will never end because the banter hasn't finished loading yet.~
@36   = ~I'm totally famous. You've probably heard of me. There's like, giant posters of me everywhere in town. I'm like, your role model aren't I?~
@37   = ~Me just guard, bother someone else little one.~
@38   = ~Me will crush, crush you to goo!~
@39   = ~You wish a short life?~
@40   = ~Greetings mercenary! My name is Raven and I was wondering if you could do something for me. I promise a decent reward if you accept.~
@41   = ~What do you wish of us fair lady?~
@42   = ~Not right now, some other time perhaps.~
@43   = ~Something very dreadful has happen to me. I had a very nice old book that has been in my family for generations which has been stolen from my room. I want my book back and I will pay handsomely for its return. Will you help me?~
@44   = ~That is an atrocious thing indeed dear lady, what foul thief would do a thing like that?~
@45   = ~Very well I will be waiting here in case you change your mind.~
@46   = ~I could not really tell in the dark but I think it was either a group of dwarves or halflings judging by their size. All three of them were short and smelled of sewer. They also had a strange accent which is why I think they were either dwarves or halflings. They said something about robbing another group some where in the Temple District. Thats all I know.~
@47   = ~Very well we shall hunt down these thieves and return your book.~
@48   = ~You return and without my book I see. I have nothing further to say to you until my book is recovered. Now go!~
@49   = ~I see you have my book. Thank you very much for returning it to me.~
@50   = ~I did promise you a reward for returning my book. Here take this, I have little use for gold.~
@51   = ~I do thank you for getting my book back but I can not be disturbed while I am studying the secrets in the book. Please leave me to my reading.~
@52   = ~Hey don't click me I don't want any trouble! Uh I know you, you're that bastard that killed Marl.~ [DUNKN02]
@53   = ~Dunkin what are you doing here?~
@54   = ~None of your business killer. Just leave me to my drink or I'll call the guard.~
@55   = ~I'm ignoring you. Go away.~
@56   = ~Yes? Is there something that I can do for you? Not to be rude, but you and your friends do not look like the kind of patronage who could afford the rates in my fine tavern. Only the wealthy and high standing citizens can afford to socialize here.~
@57   = ~For a dwarf you seem rather educated and rude at that.~
@58   = ~I would not even give you a half copper to stay in this dump.~
@59   = ~Dump you say? I will have you know that King Azoun IV and his entourage stayed here. When you have acquired some manners you may return.~
@60   = ~Have it your way. Sorry to offend you.~
@61   = ~Why don't we teach you some manners instead.~
@62   = ~Ah yes yes, off with you!~
@63   = ~Ah yes, quite the typical response from one who is of a lowly birth status. I will suffer your foul manners no more. Guards remove this filth from my sight!~
@64   = ~Of course I am educated and why wouldn't I be? You assume that because *I* being a dwarf, that I would be an uneducated neanderthal, who drinks down barrels of swill like it was going out of style and hacks and chops anything that gets in his way correct?~
@65   = ~But...~
@66   = ~I come from a very prominent family and was tutored by the best that gold could buy. I run a very successful business and have plans on branching out, perhaps even adventure in a different form of business that is unrelated to tavern management.~
@67   = ~Then we have you, the typical "adventurer". You are poorly dressed, have not bathed in months judging by your foul stench, you will do any kind of mundane quest like fetch some trinket and recieve a little reward like a good dog. Perhaps kill a barn full of rats and get 5 gold pieces for your efforts? Do not stand there with your mouth open, you will let the flies in.~
@68   = ~(You are lost for words.)~
@69   = ~The "mighty" noble adventurer has returned and what do I owe this "honor"?~
@70   = ~We need a room and do be quick about showing it to us.~
@71   = ~I had enough of your arrogant ilk. It's time to show you some manners!~
@72   = ~Ahh nothing at the moment. Perhaps some other time.~
@73   = ~Watch that tongue of yours before I have Bruno here take it from you. Now here is what I have.~
@74   = ~Why me Moradin, why me? Boys time to take out the rubbish.~
